{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"362e9f66bf03a952","type":"text","text":"[summary]\n\nThis course is designed for adult learners interested in leveraging ChatGPT and other Generative AI Large Language Models (LLMs) to enhance financial management and compliance reporting within companies. It is an asynchronous, self-paced course that combines theoretical knowledge with practical applications, enabling learners to understand and implement AI-driven solutions in their workplace effectively.\n\n### Learning Objectives\n\nBy the end of this course, participants will be able to:\n\n1. Understand the fundamentals of ChatGPT and Generative AI LLMs.\n2. Apply ChatGPT and Generative AI tools in financial management processes.\n3. Utilize AI-driven solutions for compliance and reporting requirements.\n4. Evaluate the impact of AI technologies on financial strategies and compliance frameworks.\n5. Develop a roadmap for integrating AI tools into their organization's financial and compliance operations.\n\n### Course Modules\n\n#### Introduction to ChatGPT and Generative AI\n\n- Potential benefits and challenges of Generative AI in relation to compliance and regulations.\n\n#### Understanding and Communicating with ChatGPT\n\n- Taking complex regulations and compliance, and using ChatGPT to better understand/apply it strategically\n\t- how to\n- Enhancing decision-making processes with AI-generated insights related to compliance and regulations.\n\t- how to\n- Using ChatGPT to better communicate to different stakeholders\n\t- How to\n\n \n #### Compliance and Reporting with Generative AI\n\n- Role of Generative AI in improving compliance processes.\n\t- how to\n- Generating accurate and timely compliance reports.\n\t- how to\n- Addressing regulatory challenges using ChatGPT\n\t- how to\n#### Implementing AI Solutions\n\n- Best practices for integrating AI into financial and compliance workflows\n\t- how to\n- Managing data privacy and security concerns\n\t- how to\n- Training teams and fostering an AI-ready culture.\n\t- how to\n\n#### Future Trends and Ethical Considerations\n\n- Exploring the future landscape of AI in finance and compliance. (specific or new laws, considering risk)\n- Ethical considerations and responsible use of AI technologies\n- Preparing for emerging AI trends and innovations.","x":-1560,"y":-194,"width":540,"height":914},
		{"id":"b721d13b70d028de","type":"text","text":"[topic]\nGenerative AI, ChatGPT, Data Analysis with {{[[Synthbrain/02 -🧙🏿‍♂️ Learning Lab/👨🏻‍🏫 Courses/YU/Courses/AI for Financial Management Research/ChatGPT Code Interpreter]]}}, Financial Management at companies, Compliance, Reporting\n\nOMIT topics related specific to financial management related to banking, or investing. This is a broad course on managing finances within a company.","x":-960,"y":-194,"width":280,"height":794},
		{"id":"61eba20dfe5938a4","type":"text","text":"[KB]\n{{[[Synthbrain/02 -🧙🏿‍♂️ Learning Lab/👨🏻‍🏫 Courses/YU/Courses/AI for Financial Management Research/chatgpt and financial management]]}}\n{{[[Synthbrain/02 -🧙🏿‍♂️ Learning Lab/👨🏻‍🏫 Courses/YU/Courses/AI for Financial Management Research/using code interpreter for financial projects]]}}\n{{[[Synthbrain/02 -🧙🏿‍♂️ Learning Lab/👨🏻‍🏫 Courses/YU/Courses/AI for Financial Management Research/what are some limitations of using chatgpt for financial reporting]]}}\n{{[[Synthbrain/02 -🧙🏿‍♂️ Learning Lab/👨🏻‍🏫 Courses/YU/Courses/AI for Financial Management Research/what are some examples of financial reports that chatgpt can generate]]}}\n{{[[Synthbrain/02 -🧙🏿‍♂️ Learning Lab/👨🏻‍🏫 Courses/YU/Courses/AI for Financial Management Research/what are some specific tasks that chatgpt can help with in financial management]]}}\n{{[[Synthbrain/02 -🧙🏿‍♂️ Learning Lab/👨🏻‍🏫 Courses/YU/Courses/AI for Financial Management Research/what are some examples of financial reports that chatgpt can generate]]}}\n{{[[Synthbrain/02 -🧙🏿‍♂️ Learning Lab/👨🏻‍🏫 Courses/YU/Courses/AI for Financial Management Research/ChatGPT Code Interpreter]]}}\n{{[[Synthbrain/02 -🧙🏿‍♂️ Learning Lab/👨🏻‍🏫 Courses/YU/Courses/AI for Financial Management Research/how could the chatgpt code interpreter be applied in financial management of a business]]}}\n{{[[Synthbrain/02 -🧙🏿‍♂️ Learning Lab/👨🏻‍🏫 Courses/YU/Courses/AI for Financial Management Research/ChatGPT Code Interpreter]]}}\n\nLearners will require a ChatGPT+ Account, with access to the advanced data analysis function.\n\nLearners will NOT be training their own models, only uses ones that already exist.","x":-41,"y":-194,"width":721,"height":754},
		{"id":"cb0c5985b7580195","type":"text","text":"[course]\n{{[[AI For Financial Management (Course)]]}}","x":-340,"y":109,"width":250,"height":264},
		{"id":"fd15b5781ca74dcf","type":"text","text":"[mod]\nModule 4\n","x":-620,"y":109,"width":250,"height":127},
		{"id":"b899d8fd05e60755","type":"text","text":"[Tone]\nProfessional, educational, engaging, practical.\n\nShow don't tell.","x":-620,"y":-194,"width":250,"height":220},
		{"id":"e4ce0f2c27c7ebf7","type":"text","text":"[skills]\n\n1. **Strategic AI Integration Skills**: The ability to develop and implement strategies for incorporating AI technologies into existing financial systems and workflows. This includes understanding the technical requirements, potential challenges, and steps for successful integration.\n    \n2. **Analytical Skills**: Proficiency in analyzing the impact of Generative AI on strategic financial decision-making processes. This involves evaluating how AI can influence resource allocation, forecasting, budgeting, and other critical financial decisions.\n    \n3. **Innovative Thinking**: The capability to explore and identify how AI can shape future financial strategies and drive innovations within the company. This skill requires a forward-thinking approach, considering emerging AI trends and their potential applications in finance.\n    \n4. **Ethical Framework Design**: The ability to design and implement a framework for ethical decision-making in AI applications. This includes understanding and addressing issues related to accountability, fairness, transparency, and the potential for bias in AI-driven financial decisions.\n    \n5. **Critical Thinking**: Enhanced critical thinking skills to evaluate the benefits and limitations of AI in financial management, ensuring that strategic decisions are made based on a comprehensive understanding of AI capabilities and ethical considerations.\n    \n6. **Problem-Solving Skills**: The ability to identify and solve complex problems that may arise during the integration of AI into financial systems, including technical, ethical, and strategic challenges.\n    \n7. **Communication Skills**: Proficiency in communicating the strategic value of AI integration to stakeholders, including explaining complex AI concepts in understandable terms and articulating the benefits and potential risks of AI-driven financial strategies.\n    \n8. **Adaptability and Continuous Learning**: The skill to adapt to rapidly evolving AI technologies and their applications in finance, demonstrating a commitment to continuous learning and staying abreast of the latest developments in AI and financial management.\n\n","x":895,"y":-823,"width":810,"height":1064},
